  "details": "We should have the ability to force people to load our fallback avatars by default based on safety settings. This prevents people, randos, non-friends to load and scrape or 'rip' the avatar data of everyone in the instance by simply joining. \nThe idea being if they are not friends, manually enabled or whatever safety setting option is enabled, only a fallback avatar will be loaded instead of the person's actual main avatar, thus the legion of desktopping avatar rippers fueling the edgy ripped avatar scene can't just trawl public worlds, downloading avatar data en masse.",
